---
<section class="block" id="operate">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head rv">
      <h2>Operate it like infrastructure</h2>
      <p>Install once, run as a daemon, reload maps without dropping connections. Everything is inspectable.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ops-grid rv">
      <div class="op">
        <h3>Foreground</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo albus run</code></pre>
        <p>Defaults are deliberate. Overrides are flags, not config files.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="op">
        <h3>Daemon</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo albus service install
sudo albus service start</code></pre>
        <p>One unprivileged service user, scoped capabilities, clean stop-cleanup.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="op">
        <h3>Observe</h3>
        <pre><code>albus status --json
albus monitor</code></pre>
        <p>Machine-readable status for bars and panels; live telemetry TUI for driving.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="op">
        <h3>Reconfigure</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo albus service reload</code></pre>
        <p>SIGHUP re-reads configuration and hot-reloads eBPF maps with zero downtime.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="op-note rv">
      Requires Linux 5.10+ with <code>CONFIG_BPF</code>, cgroup v2 and Rust 1.89. One static binary, no containers, no relay, no account.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ops-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 24px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .ops-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .op {
    border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 22px 24px; background: var(--surface);
  }
  .op h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 16px; }
  .op pre {
    margin: 0 0 14px; padding: 10px 12px; background: #000;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .op p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13.5px; }
  .op-note { margin-top: 36px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13.5px; max-width: 720px; }
  .op-note code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--ink); }
</style>
